# Gate step 2243-wosv — the Lua runner's stdin primitive: a script reads its
# own stdin only when its header says `-- @stdin <max-bytes>`; the read is
# bounded (refused:stdin:too-large:<cap>) and EOF-safe (a closed stdin is "",
# at once), so no decider the door runs can block a gate on an inherited stdin.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
